) use exponent s*A-K and s*B-K. At the final choice s=2n/beta, Cauchy-Schwarz of those displayed bounds controls exp((n/beta)*(A+B-2K/s)), not the printed exp((n/beta)*Z); an extra K/2 remains. This confirms the local split-penalty bookkeeping mismatch pointed out in target p.60. Replacing -K/s by -2K/s and correspondingly strengthening the deterministic coefficient conditions is a possible repair. It does not by itself disprove LR2014 Theorem A or certify all constants of the repaired theorem."},{"claim_id":"V06_current_signed_term_repair","evidence":[{"locator":"PDF physical page 59","read_range":"PDF physical page 59","source_id":"702a85c49e575d27470d1b12f997e26fe37b32a99058ea42315574c997de3b6b"},{"locator":"PDF physical page 60","read_range":"PDF physical page 60","source_id":"702a85c49e575d27470d1b12f997e26fe37b32a99058ea42315574c997de3b6b"}],"kind":"inference","suggested_label":"U","text":"For c=eta+kappa and A=1+8mu/(c-12mu)<=2, replacing A*Z by 2*Z alone needs care because Z can be negative. Current p.59 supplies Z>=-3mu*V-2K/s. Substitution while retaining the remaining V and K terms leaves coefficients 5mu-c/4<=0 and 4/s-1/(lambda*n)<=0. Thus this particular signed-term step can be completed under the printed constraints; it is not a counterexample to Theorem 4."},{"claim_id":"V07_coarse_branch_present","evidence":[{"locator":"PDF physical page 23","read_range":"PDF physical page 23","source_id":"702a85c49e575d27470d1b12f997e26fe37b32a99058ea42315574c997de3b6b"},{"locator":"PDF physical page 27","read_range":"PDF physical page 27","source_id":"702a85c49e575d27470d1b12f997e26fe37b32a99058ea42315574c997de3b6b"}],"kind":"direct_evidence","suggested_label":"U","text":"Current p.27 contains the coarse-grid branch, then explicitly combines fine and coarse instances to conclude Theorem 5. It was missing from both earlier selected-page Pro packets, not absent from the paper. The branch uses a gap interval in the fixed uniform grid to exclude the target-optimal mid